# Settings a DocKitty site reads from its env files. Nothing here is secret.
#
# This file is an example: no build reads `.env.example`. Copy the line you need
# into an env file the build does read, in the site directory (next to
# astro.config.mjs):
#
#   .env                      every build and the dev server
#   .env.production           `astro build` and `astro preview` only
#   .env.development          `astro dev` only
#   .env.local, .env.<mode>.local   the same, for one machine; keep them out of git
#
# A value in the process environment wins over every file.

# Draft publication. A page is a draft when its frontmatter says
# `doc_status: draft` or has no `doc_status`.
#
#   on   (default) drafts are built, listed in the sidebar and marked `noindex`.
#   off  drafts are not built. Set this for the live site.
#
# For a live deployment, put the line below (uncommented) in `.env.production`,
# or set DK_PUBLISH_DRAFTS=off in the environment of the deploy job, as this
# repository's .github/workflows/deploy.yml does.
# DK_PUBLISH_DRAFTS=off
